termination_clause:
9. TERMINATION 

9.1 Termination by Either Party . This Agreement may be terminated by either party upon written notice to the other in accordance with Section 10.1 if:

(a) The other party shall have committed a material breach of any term or condition of this Agreement and such breach is not cured within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice thereof from the non-breaching party; 

(b) The other party shall have made an assignment for the benefit of creditors, filed a petition in bankruptcy or been adjudicated bankrupt or insolvent;

(c) A receiver or trustee has been appointed to take possession of all or substantially all of the property of the other party and such appointment is not vacated within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice thereof from the non-breaching party; 

(d) The other party shall have dissolved, liquidated or otherwise ceased to exist.

9.2 Termination by NCM . In addition to the foregoing, this Agreement may be terminated by NCM upon written notice to Network Affiliate if:

(a) Network Affiliate fails to pay any amount due and owing under this Agreement within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice thereof from NCM; 

(b) Network Affiliate shall have failed to comply with any material provision of Section 2.1, 2.3 or 2.5.

9.3 Termination by Network Affiliate . In addition to the foregoing, this Agreement may be terminated by Network Affiliate upon written notice to NCM if:

(a) NCM fails to deliver the Service in accordance with the terms and conditions of this Agreement for a period of thirty (30) consecutive days; 

(b) NCM shall have failed to comply with any material provision of Section 2.1, 2.3 or 2.5.

9.4 Termination Upon Expiration . This Agreement will automatically expire upon the expiration of the Term as defined in Section 8.1.

9.5 Effect of Termination . Upon termination of this Agreement for any reason:

(a) All rights and obligations of the parties hereunder shall cease;

(b) Network Affiliate shall immediately pay to NCM all amounts due and owing under this Agreement, including without limitation, all capital costs and other expenses incurred by NCM in connection with the installation and maintenance of the Equipment; 

(c) NCM shall remove from the Theatres all NCM Property.

9.6 Survival . Notwithstanding termination or expiration of this Agreement for any reason, the following provisions will survive: Sections 1, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10 and 11.

9.7 Cancellation Fee . In the event that Network Affiliate terminates this Agreement prior to the end of the Term, Network Affiliate shall pay NCM a cancellation fee equal to one hundred percent (100%) of all capital costs incurred by NCM in connection with the installation and maintenance of the Equipment.

