termination_clause:
12.2 TERMINATION

12.2.1 Termination by Harpoon

Harpoon may terminate this Agreement upon written notice to Janssen if:

(a) Janssen commits a material breach of any term or condition of this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice from Harpoon specifying the breach and requiring its cure;

(b) Janssen makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors, files a petition in bankruptcy or is adjudicated bankrupt or insolvent; 

(c) Janssen dissolves or liquidates, or enters into any dissolution or liquidation agreement with its creditors.

12.2.2 Termination by Janssen

Janssen may terminate this Agreement upon written notice to Harpoon if:

(a) Harpoon commits a material breach of any term or condition of this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within thirty (30) days after receipt of written notice from Janssen specifying the breach and requiring its cure;

(b) Harpoon makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors, files a petition in bankruptcy or is adjudicated bankrupt or insolvent; 

(c) Harpoon dissolves or liquidates, or enters into any dissolution or liquidation agreement with its creditors.

12.2.3 Termination by Regulatory Action

Either Party may terminate this Agreement upon written notice to the other if:

(a) the Regulatory Authorities revoke or suspend any Regulatory Approval for a Licensed Product; 

(b) the Regulatory Authorities impose a material restriction on the marketing, sale or distribution of a Licensed Product.

12.2.4 Termination by Mutual Consent

Either Party may terminate this Agreement upon mutual written consent of both Parties.

12.3 EFFECT OF TERMINATION

Upon termination of this Agreement:

(a) all rights and obligations of the Parties under this Agreement shall cease;

(b) Harpoon shall promptly return to Janssen any Confidential Information in its possession or control;

(c) Janssen shall promptly return to Harpoon any Confidential Information in its possession or control.

12.4 SURVIVAL

The following provisions shall survive termination of this Agreement:

(a) Articles 1, 7 and 13; 

(b) all obligations of the Parties under Articles 2 through 6 that by their nature are intended to survive termination;

(c) any other provision that is reasonably necessary for the interpretation or enforcement of this Agreement.

12.5 BANKRUPTCY

If either Party files a petition in bankruptcy, makes an assignment for the benefit of creditors, dissolves or liquidates, or enters into any dissolution or liquidation agreement with its creditors, then:

(a) the other Party may terminate this Agreement upon written notice to such Party;

(b) all rights and obligations of the Parties under this Agreement shall cease.

12.6 GOVERNING LAW

The laws of the State of New York shall govern this Section 12.

